                        "entry_id": "23e79eb6-e643-34f4-9feb-4066143b7597",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Obsolete form of immantle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bcf1c381-10c8-4a2b-b78b-ca0aee29c3a4",
                                "sense_id": "ccf5b164-dbd9-3b13-8d0e-0a42048cd848",
                                "text": "The World, and this, which by another name men have thought good to call Heaven (under the pourprise and bending cope wherof, all things are emmanteled and covered) beleeve wee ought in all reason to be a God, eternall, unmeasurable, without beginning, and likewise endlesse."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e941b38f-2d87-30cb-8426-9db424544235",
                        "entry_id": "23e79eb6-e643-34f4-9feb-4066143b7597",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Place around as a fortification"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "72e243b9-9fce-4785-8b18-84952ff90a6e",
                                "sense_id": "e941b38f-2d87-30cb-8426-9db424544235",
                                "text": "Whereby he grew to such wealth, that of late he bequeathed by his last will and testament ten millions of Sesterces unto his native city Marsils toward the fortifications therof, besides the walls that he caused to be built and emmanteled about other towns , which cost him little under the foresaid summe."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
